# The census is one name per line, so Git keeps both sides' lines on a merge
# instead of a conflict and one landed PR does not block the next. A union keeps
# every line from both sides, not only additions: a name classified differently
# by each side, or a row left for a utility the other side removed, is failed by
# tools/check-utility-census.py (also run by check-adaptation-boundary.sh).
tools/adaptation-census.tsv merge=union
